.TH REC2SQL "1" "April 2026" "GNU recutils 1.9.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rec2sql \- rec to sql converter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rec2sql
[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR]... [\fI\,REC_FILE\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Convert rec data into SQL INSERT statements.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-type\fR=\fI\,TYPE\/\fR
record set to convert; if this parameter
is omitted then the default record set is used
.TP
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-table\fR=\fI\,NAME\/\fR
use NAME as the SQL table name instead of
the record type
.TP
\fB\-S\fR, \fB\-\-sort\fR=\fI\,FIELDS\/\fR
sort the output by the specified fields.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
print a help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
show version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Convert all records to SQL INSERT statements:

  rec2sql contacts.rec

Convert a specific record type:

  rec2sql -t Task todo.rec

Use a custom table name:

  rec2sql -t Task -T tasks_table todo.rec

Pipe output into SQLite:

  rec2sql contacts.rec | sqlite3 contacts.db
